    {
      "name": "run_script",
      "description": "Run a sandboxed Lua 5.4 script on-device. The script can call the same pin/power/lock tools as MCP (not run_script). Optional maxCalls and timeout (microseconds) must not exceed firmware ceilings. One script at a time.\n\nLua 5.4. Allowed libraries: base, table, string, math, utf8. require, dofile, loadfile, load, and collectgarbage are nil. No io, os, package, debug, or coroutine.\n\nEach tool is a global that takes one argument table with the same keys as MCP (always pass pins even for one pin). JSON arrays become 1-based Lua tables. sleep(us) delays in microseconds and counts toward timeout, not maxCalls. print() is captured as output. The first return value is result (JSON).\n\nErrors raise a table {reason=\"...\"}. Catch with pcall and read err.reason. Uncaught errors fail the request with that reason; print output is discarded.\n\nCatchable with pcall:\n- Tool failure: system sentence (no \"The script reported\" prefix), e.g. pin/lock/mode errors\n- error(\"msg\"): \"The script reported an error: msg. Catch it with pcall or fix the script.\"\n- error() or error(\"\"): \"The script called error with no message. Catch it with pcall or fix the script.\"\n\nNot catchable (abort the whole run even if pcall returns):\n- timeout: \"Script exceeded timeout.\"\n- maxCalls: \"Script exceeded maxCalls.\"\n- out of memory: \"Script ran out of memory.\"\n- syntax or uncaught Lua runtime: \"The script failed: <message>. Catch it with pcall or fix the script.\"\n\nExample:\nconfigure_pins{pins={0}, mode=\"digitalOutput\", pullUp=false, pullDown=false}\nset_pin_levels{pins={0}, level=1}\nsleep(5000)\nlocal r = get_pin_levels{pins={0}}\nprint(\"level\", r.levels[1])\nreturn r\n\nError handling:\nlocal ok, err = pcall(function()\n  set_pin_levels{pins={0}, level=1}\nend)\nif not ok then\n  return {ok=false, reason=err.reason}\nend",
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": false,
        "openWorldHint": false
      },
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "script"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "script": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 8192,
            "description": "Lua 5.4 source. Allowed libraries: base, table, string, math, utf8.",
            "examples": [
              "configure_pins{pins={0}, mode=\"digitalOutput\", pullUp=false, pullDown=false}\nset_pin_levels{pins={0}, level=1}\nsleep(5000)\nlocal r = get_pin_levels{pins={0}}\nprint(\"level\", r.levels[1])\nreturn r"
            ]
          },
          "maxCalls": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 256,
            "description": "Max tool invocations this run"
          },
          "timeout": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 10000000,
            "description": "Wall-clock budget in microseconds"
          },
          "lockId": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/lockId"
          }
        },
        "$defs": {
          "lockId": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "description": "Required when another lock holds the resource."
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
